H1 Type Declaration Instruction

This instruction is used to declare the type of each variable being used in the program. Any variable used in the program must be declared before using it in any statement.

Book - pg55

The following statements would work:
    int a, b, c, d ; //here, ints are declared and ready to use.
    a = b = c = 10 ;
However, the following statement would not work:
    int a = b = c = d = 10 ; // here value can't be assigned during declaration

See how Java reads the line

    int a, b, c, d ; //it is declared here
    a = b = c = 10 ; //and here
    (a = (b = (c=10))) // program knows c is already declared and ready to get a value.
    (a = (b = 10)) // program knows b is already declared and ready to get a value.
    (a = 10) // program knows a is already declared and ready to get a value.

But,

    int a = b = c = d = 10 ; // here value can't be assigned during declaration

    int a = (b = (c = (d = 10))); //d is not declared, it'll give error declaration works from the beginning.
    and a is still blank.

